From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:15:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kms: shut down after the pointer stops reaching the cursor
 manager

KMS drops its cursor manager when the backend prepares to shut down,
and its handler was connected before the native cursor renderer's,
which is what stops the input thread from handing it pointer
positions. Moving the pointer in between had the input thread call
into a cursor manager that was already gone, and the compositor
crashed on the way out. KMS now prepares to shut down after the
handlers of everything that feeds it.

Fixes https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/4652

Upstream-Status: forwardable
---
 src/backends/native/meta-kms.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-kms.c b/src/backends/native/meta-kms.c
index ad58cea26583d1bc2dad3fc0d3c833d26b6fac56..634991b3b0250ce0eb3de97cca77163cf61bc35f 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms.c
@@ -479,9 +479,9 @@ meta_kms_new (MetaBackend   *backend,
     g_signal_connect (udev, "device-removed",
                       G_CALLBACK (on_udev_device_removed), kms);
 
-  g_signal_connect (backend, "prepare-shutdown",
-                    G_CALLBACK (on_prepare_shutdown),
-                    kms);
+  g_signal_connect_after (backend, "prepare-shutdown",
+                          G_CALLBACK (on_prepare_shutdown),
+                          kms);
 
   return kms;
 }
